263
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:12,170
The Japan team's last hope is in the Tachibana brothers' Space Storm.

264
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:14,750
Catch, here it comes!

265
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:16,210
Yes!

266
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:18,800
Twin Shot!

267
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,840
I won't allow it!

268
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:25,550
Oh, the Tachibana twins' shot,

269
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:29,100
is deflected by Pierre-kun's extraordinary move!

270
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:30,560
Great, Pierre!

271
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,560
I saw this trick before in the Argentina match.

272
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:37,360
As long as I'm here, you can't score.

273
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:41,360
This last trick of Japan is also not a goal!

274
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,860
Pierre-kun stands like a solid wall between them and the French goal.

275
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:46,410
Great, Pierre!

276
00:15:46,490 --> 00:15:48,080
We've won this match!

277
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,910
Referee, blow the whistle, it's time.

278
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,830
This is not good.

279
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,580
The Tachibana brothers' Space Storm also didn't work.

280
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,670
The kids are marking numbers 9, 10, and 12.

281
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:05,760
And now I also stopped numbers 2 and 3.

282
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:09,510
The Japan team no longer has any long-distance shooters.

283
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:12,060
We won!

284
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:15,230
The referee looks at his watch!

285
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:18,310
The match has entered injury time.

286
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:23,190
Will Pierre-kun's tremendous effort carry France to the final?

287
00:16:23,530 --> 00:16:25,950
Not yet! We haven't lost yet.

288
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,450
Oh, but Misaki-kun is there.

289
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:31,040
He picks up the ball that Pierre-kun cleared.

290
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:35,960
On this muddy ground, he charges alone toward France's goal.

291
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:39,960
This is the final attack for Japan.

292
00:16:40,550 --> 00:16:41,380
He!

293
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:42,880
- Misaki!\N- Misaki-kun!

294
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,300
- Taro!\N- Misaki!

295
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,590
Misaki-kun!

296
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:48,590
Japan no longer has long-distance shooters.

297
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:51,470
That's why Misaki-kun tries to infiltrate by dribbling.

298
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:56,480
In the current conditions, dribbling is almost impossible, but will he succeed?

299
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:58,860
Bring it on, Misaki.

300
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:02,320
No matter what the ground is like, we play on equal terms.

301
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,360
If dribbling is hard, defending is also hard.

302
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:09,950
France is the host country, they have taken professional Pierre and

303
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:13,620
formed a team consisting of elite players who have been playing together for months.

304
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:21,170
Whereas our Japan team was hastily put together with different players.

305
00:17:22,710 --> 00:17:28,180
But our hearts have had the same goal for three years.

306
00:17:28,430 --> 00:17:29,470
And that goal...

307
00:17:30,430 --> 00:17:33,140
I want to go to Brazil and become a professional!

308
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:36,430
And make Japan number one in the world.

309
00:17:36,850 --> 00:17:38,390
Those words...

310
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:43,400
affected me, Wakabayashi-kun, Kojiro, and likewise Matsuyama.

311
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:49,110
There is no doubt that Tsubasa-kun's words that day affected all of us.

312
00:17:50,410 --> 00:17:52,120
Misaki-kun gets past!

313
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:56,410
Even in the worst conditions, Misaki-kun's technique still shines.

314
00:17:56,870 --> 00:17:58,290
Three years have passed since then.

315
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:02,090
We have started to take our step toward the goal of becoming number one in the world.

316
00:18:02,170 --> 00:18:05,760
Winning this tournament will be our first big step.

317
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:10,680
We cannot lose in the semifinal, we do not lose.

318
00:18:10,970 --> 00:18:12,430
It's impossible for us to lose!

319
00:18:12,510 --> 00:18:17,180
Incredible! Misaki-kun passes the entire France team.

320
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:18,890
What magnificent play.

321
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:22,650
Despite the state of the ground, his ball control is wonderful.

322
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,190
So does Japan have one more person,

323
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:28,190
who dribbles like Ozora Tsubasa?

324
00:18:28,490 --> 00:18:30,450
Good luck, Misaki!

325
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:33,200
We will win! We will win!

326
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:36,740
When this tournament is over, I will be alone again.

327
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:40,290
I won't be able to play football with these kids again.

328
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:44,210
I may be in France, but I am Japanese.

329
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:49,300
From now on, I want to represent Japan, I will wear this flag and fight.

330
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,220
Look at me.

331
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:53,550
Dad!

332
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:55,470
Taro.

333
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:59,270
The referee looks at his watch.

334
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:01,310
Only a few seconds left.

335
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:04,270
And there is one person left from the France team.

336
00:19:04,650 --> 00:19:06,860
Pierre-kun is waiting!

337
00:19:07,070 --> 00:19:09,030
The man who spoiled Matsuyama-kun's Eagle Shot

338
00:19:09,110 --> 00:19:12,280
and the Tachibana brothers' Space Storm.

339
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:16,660
El Sid Pierre blocks the path to the French goal.

340
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:21,750
One-on-one. Let's settle it here, Misaki.

341
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,880
Bring it on, Pierre.

342
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:27,000
This is the final gamble.

343
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:33,260
Oh, Misaki-kun kicks the ball behind Pierre-kun.

344
00:19:33,550 --> 00:19:34,390
What?

345
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:37,510
But his kick was very weak.

346
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:41,680
Oh, the ball stops in a puddle.

347
00:19:41,770 --> 00:19:44,650
Misaki-kun suddenly runs at speed.

348
00:19:44,730 --> 00:19:46,940
Pierre-kun also turns and chases after him.

349
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,440
The goalkeeper also comes out.

350
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:51,190
Pierre turned and then ran.

351
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:53,740
Whereas I must accelerate thanks to my dribbling.

352
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,660
I will reach the ball first!

353
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:59,120
And then it's over!

354
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:05,330
What happened! Misaki-kun slides on the ground with a tackle to increase his speed.

355
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:08,210
This is Misaki-kun's tackle shot.

356
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:10,210
- Good!\N- You did it, Misaki!

357
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,220
Not yet, I'm here!

358
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:16,720
Napoleon comes from the side and blocks him.

359
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,720
Japan cannot score on their final attack.

360
00:20:21,810 --> 00:20:23,730
- Napoleon!\N- Well done!

361
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,770
I can't do it! There is no chance left.

362
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:28,730
Don't give up, Misaki-kun!

363
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:34,280
Tsubasa-kun comes from behind...

364
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,610
and presses on Misaki-kun's blocked foot.

365
00:20:36,910 --> 00:20:41,120
They break Napoleon's barricade! The Golden Duo is in good shape.

366
00:20:41,410 --> 00:20:42,410
Good.

367
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:45,620
Misaki-kun jumps.

368
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:50,170
And immediately on the ball in the air,

369
00:20:50,710 --> 00:20:52,510
he makes an overhead kick!

370
00:20:54,130 --> 00:20:58,760
Goal! Misaki-kun's shot enters France's goal!

371
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,930
We... did it Misaki! We tied it up.

372
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,270
No!

373
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:08,270
Not a goal! The match had ended before the goal!

374
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:14,030
Was that whistle for the goal or the whistle signaling the end of the match?

375
00:21:14,110 --> 00:21:18,360
If it's the latter, the score is 4-3 and France advances to the final.

376
00:21:20,530 --> 00:21:21,870
The goal is valid.

377
00:21:24,540 --> 00:21:29,040
The goal is valid! Misaki-kun's shot is accepted.

378
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:33,550
The Japan team stubbornly scored just before the end of the match.

379
00:21:33,630 --> 00:21:36,970
Now the score is 4-4 and it's a draw.

380
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:40,800
The match goes into two 10-minute extra time periods.

381
00:21:40,930 --> 00:21:45,060
- You were great, Misaki.\N- Hooray, Misaki, you took a great shot.

382
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:47,350
He did it, they tied it up.

383
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,560
It's a draw, it's a draw.

384
00:21:50,150 --> 00:21:52,190
Well done, Taro.

385
00:21:52,570 --> 00:21:53,900
Great.

386
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:59,780
Now I can play football with Tsubasa-kun and the others for 20 more minutes.

387
00:22:00,410 --> 00:22:01,570
Misaki-kun.

388
00:23:46,130 --> 00:23:49,960
Next Episode: Extra Time in the Rain